<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!--
    Sponsors for the events you host (James, 2026-10-29): who offers, what they ask and what they
    pay. Read by EqSponsorship; balance changes need no code.

    Every sponsor is a brand from the player's own shop, read when the game runs: no brand is
    named here except the ones left out below. A brand's size comes from what it sells:
    first how many shop categories it has machines in, then how many price bands they span, then
    how many machines. So a brand can be small in one game and big in another with mods.

    sponsors
        offerMonths     offers stay this many months after the start of the year (or after they
                        first appear in a save), then go until next year
        cancelShare     cancelling early costs this share of one event's fee for each year left
                        (a part year counts as a whole)
        missFactor      the fee for the next contract year after a missed yearly target
        missesToLeave   missed targets in a row before the sponsor walks away
        machinesMax     the most of its machines any sponsor asks the farm to own (each size
                        has its own, lower or equal)
        attachmentWeight  how much one attachment or trailer of the sponsor's counts toward the
                        machines to own (James, 2026-11-01: a cheap header shouldn't count as
                        a whole machine); anything that drives itself counts 1
        maxSponsors     the most sponsors a farm can sign at once (James, 2026-10-31: up to
                        three, each with all its rules met). An exclusive sponsor is always the
                        only one, and no two sponsors may share a shop category
        discountMonths  months after signing before a sponsor's repair, repaint and buying
                        discounts start (James, 2026-11-01: 3)

    easyCategories      shop categories of machines that are easy to get (tractors, cars,
                        trucks, telehandlers, loaders): a brand with one of them needs only the
                        size's minItemsEasy machines in the shop instead of minItems (James,
                        2026-10-31). Names are matched without case; unknown names do nothing

    skipCategoryTypes   shop category types (the shop's groups, such as DRIVABLES, TRAILERS or
                        SOIL_PREPARATION) whose items are no machines; every other group counts.
                        Placeables and hand tools are left out anyway
    skipBrands          brands never offered: the game's "no brand", and Lizard, the game's own
                        brand, which James keeps for a surprise one-off sponsor later
    priceBands          upper edges of the price bands a brand's machines are spread over; the
                        last band has no top

    size                name (small, moderate, big), share of the brands ranked by size, offers
                        made each year, contract years (min to max), fee per event (min to max
                        before strictness), popularity points it brings to a sponsored event,
                        its yearly popularity target before strictness, and the event rating it
                        sponsors from (minRating), with a share of the fee at the rating below
                        (lowerShare, 0 for none) and the lowest rating that share is paid at
                        (lowerRating), and the fewest shop machines a brand needs for that size
                        (minItems: a brand short of it drops to a smaller size, and one short of
                        every size is never a sponsor; minItemsEasy for a brand with an easy
                        category, minItems when left out), and the chance an offer is exclusive
                        (exclusive: 1 always, 0 never), and the chance an offer lends a
                        machine for each event month it backs (loan: 1 always, 0 never)

    loans               sponsors that lend (James, 2026-11-01): on the first day of an event
                        month they back, each delivers one of its machines to the dealer, leased
                        to the farm for free (no leasing costs, free repairs: its price is 0) and
                        taken back when the month ends. The farm can use it for anything, plinths
                        included. top = the share of the brand's machines, dearest first, it
                        picks from (self-driven ones when it has any); always = brands that lend
                        whenever they sponsor, like Lizard's one-off sponsorship

    strictness          each offer rolls a strictness from 0 (Relaxed) to 1 (Hard bargain); every
                        term and reward runs from its "relaxed" value to its "strict" one, then
                        a small wobble (+- wobble, a share) keeps two offers apart
        word            the deal words, by strictness (from = the lowest strictness for that word)
        categoriesPerMachine   one of the sponsor's machines to own for this many categories it makes
        window          competitor clause: another brand's machine in a category the sponsor
                        makes, priced within this share of one of the sponsor's machines there
        target          added to the size's popularity target
        top3            from this strictness the yearly target also needs a top 3 finish
        branding        the branding level an offer requires to sign and be paid (1 Low, 2 Medium,
                        3 High), rounded
        fee             multiplies the size's fee
        repair, repaint, purchase   discounts on the sponsor's machines

    lizard              Lizard's free one-off sponsorship (EqLizard): the chance an unsponsored
                        hosted event gets an offer (rolled the month before), the popularity it
                        brings, eventingFactor times the fee for a 3 Day Event; per rating the fee
                        paid when the results come in and the branding
                        level asked for (1 Low, 2 Medium, 3 High); the bulk materials the Lizard
                        plinth may ask for (one is picked, by weight) with that plinth's shop item,
                        and the parts every plinth needs. The amounts must match
                        art/source/lizard_plinth.py, which writes them into the plinths.

    Part of Realistic Equestrian by Jasta007.
-->
<sponsors offerMonths="6" cancelShare="0.15" missFactor="0.75" missesToLeave="2" machinesMax="5" maxSponsors="3" attachmentWeight="0.5" discountMonths="3">
    <skipCategoryTypes>
        <type name="ANIMALS"/>
        <type name="OBJECTS"/>
        <type name="HANDTOOLS"/>
        <type name="MISC"/>
        <type name="PLACEABLES"/>
    </skipCategoryTypes>

    <skipBrands>
        <brand name="NONE"/>
        <brand name="LIZARD"/>
    </skipBrands>

    <loans top="0.34">
        <always brand="LIZARD"/>
    </loans>

    <easyCategories>
        <category name="tractorsS"/>
        <category name="tractorsM"/>
        <category name="tractorsL"/>
        <category name="cars"/>
        <category name="trucks"/>
        <category name="teleLoaderVehicles"/>
        <category name="frontLoaderVehicles"/>
        <category name="frontLoaders"/>
        <category name="wheelLoaderVehicles"/>
    </easyCategories>

    <priceBands>
        <band max="10000"/>
        <band max="30000"/>
        <band max="100000"/>
        <band max="300000"/>
        <band max="1000000"/>
    </priceBands>

    <sizes>
        <size name="big"      share="0.15" offers="3" yearsMin="3" yearsMax="3" feeMin="120000" feeMax="180000" popularity="10" target="70" minRating="championship" lowerShare="0.25" lowerRating="intermediate" minItems="15" machinesMax="5" exclusive="1" loan="0.6"/>
        <size name="moderate" share="0.35" offers="4" yearsMin="1" yearsMax="2" feeMin="25000"  feeMax="40000"  popularity="6"  target="55" minRating="intermediate" lowerShare="0"    lowerRating="intermediate" minItems="8"  machinesMax="3" exclusive="0.5" loan="0.4"/>
        <size name="small"    share="0.50" offers="5" yearsMin="1" yearsMax="1" feeMin="3000"   feeMax="6000"   popularity="3"  target="40" minRating="novice"       lowerShare="0"    lowerRating="novice"       minItems="3"  minItemsEasy="1" machinesMax="1" exclusive="0" loan="0.25"/>
    </sizes>

    <!-- Branding (James, 2026-10-31): sponsor boards on the farm's placeables, anywhere, make a
         level; the player sees only the word. Below an offer's required level it can't be signed
         and pays nothing; at or above it pays this share of the fee (the full fee at High). -->
    <branding>
        <level name="low"    boards="1"  pay="0.5"/>
        <level name="medium" boards="5"  pay="0.75"/>
        <level name="high"   boards="10" pay="1"/>
    </branding>

    <strictness wobble="0.1">
        <word name="relaxed"     from="0"/>
        <word name="fair"        from="0.25"/>
        <word name="demanding"   from="0.5"/>
        <word name="hardBargain" from="0.75"/>
        <term name="categoriesPerMachine" relaxed="4"    strict="2"/>
        <term name="window"               relaxed="0.2"  strict="0.6"/>
        <term name="target"               relaxed="-10"  strict="10"/>
        <term name="top3"                 from="0.75"/>
        <term name="branding"             relaxed="1"    strict="3"/>
        <term name="fee"                  relaxed="0.8"  strict="1.3"/>
        <term name="repair"               relaxed="0.15" strict="0.35"/>
        <term name="repaint"              relaxed="0.35" strict="0.65"/>
        <term name="purchase"             relaxed="0.05" strict="0.2"/>
    </strictness>

    <lizard chance="0.25" popularity="5" eventingFactor="1.5">
        <rating name="novice"       fee="6000"  branding="1"/>
        <rating name="intermediate" fee="18000" branding="2"/>
        <rating name="championship" fee="45000" branding="3"/>
        <material fillType="STONE"     amount="1000"  weight="1" xml="placeables/sponsorPlinths/lizardPlinthStone.xml"/>
        <material fillType="WOODCHIPS" amount="1000"  weight="1" xml="placeables/sponsorPlinths/lizardPlinthWoodChips.xml"/>
        <material fillType="STRAW"     amount="10000" weight="1" xml="placeables/sponsorPlinths/lizardPlinthStraw.xml"/>
        <part fillType="WOOD"   amount="10000"/>
        <part fillType="BOARDS" amount="1000"/>
    </lizard>
</sponsors>
